1
00:00:00,025 --> 00:00:07,735
For most repair shops, the customer journey begins with a phone call, and every missed call can mean a missed repair order.

2
00:00:07,735 --> 00:00:10,117
ZOL is designed to answer immediately.

3
00:00:10,117 --> 00:00:25,725
In this complete product vision, we will follow Jordan and a 2015 Chevrolet Sonic from the first conversation through diagnosis, repair, payment, and long-term customer care, while also exploring the operating tools used by managers and technicians.

4
00:00:29,822 --> 00:00:35,400
Jordan calls because the check-engine light is on and the Sonic shakes while stopped.

5
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:43,668
Ava, ZOL's AI receptionist, greets the customer, identifies the vehicle, and asks focused safety and service-intake questions.

6
00:00:43,668 --> 00:00:47,342
Ava does not make a definitive diagnosis over the phone.

7
00:00:47,342 --> 00:00:57,645
She establishes whether the warning light is steady or flashing, asks about overheating, stalling, and power loss, and provides conservative safety guidance.

8
00:00:57,645 --> 00:01:05,322
The complete conversation is transcribed automatically, so the advisor never has to reconstruct the call from memory.

9
00:01:11,975 --> 00:01:23,970
ZOL converts the transcript into structured, usable information: customer identity, vehicle, primary complaint, symptoms, urgency, requested service, preferred time, and safety advice.

10
00:01:23,970 --> 00:01:28,599
The system matches Jordan to the existing customer and vehicle records.

11
00:01:28,599 --> 00:01:41,507
It then checks the shop calendar and technician specialties, finds the earliest conflict-free diagnostic opening, assigns Marcus, reserves the bay, creates the appointment, and sends a confirmation.

12
00:01:41,507 --> 00:01:49,525
The call, transcript, extracted details, booking outcome, and confirmation become part of the customer relationship record.

13
00:01:50,670 --> 00:01:53,153
The confirmation is only the first update.

14
00:01:53,153 --> 00:01:56,464
ZOL maintains a communication journey around the repair.

15
00:01:56,464 --> 00:02:11,601
The customer can receive notifications when the appointment is confirmed, the vehicle is checked in, diagnostics are complete, an estimate is ready, work is approved, parts are ordered or received, repairs are complete, and the vehicle is ready for pickup.

16
00:02:11,601 --> 00:02:20,470
Message history stays connected to the customer and repair order, while the provider remains replaceable for SMS, email, or future voice integrations.

17
00:02:24,912 --> 00:02:36,224
Inside the shop, the live dashboard gives managers an immediate picture of appointments, vehicles in process, approvals, parts delays, pickup readiness, revenue, and technician workload.

18
00:02:36,224 --> 00:02:42,367
The calendar connects every appointment to the customer, vehicle, complaint, and assigned technician.

19
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:48,814
When Jordan arrives, the advisor records mileage, fuel, visible damage, notes, and photos where available.

20
00:02:48,814 --> 00:02:56,112
Check-in creates the repair order automatically and preserves the original call details as the work moves into the shop.

21
00:03:01,340 --> 00:03:05,532
ZOL maintains a connected profile for every customer and vehicle.

22
00:03:05,532 --> 00:03:16,561
The shop can review contact preferences, vehicles, past visits, messages, invoices, payments, declined work, upcoming maintenance, lifetime value, and now AI call history.

23
00:03:16,561 --> 00:03:22,753
Vehicle records preserve mileage, inspections, diagnostics, recommendations, and repair history.

24
00:03:22,753 --> 00:03:34,040
Global search can find a customer name, license plate, VIN, vehicle description, repair-order number, appointment, or invoice and take the user directly to the correct record.

25
00:03:48,527 --> 00:03:52,056
The repair order is the operational center of ZOL.

26
00:03:52,056 --> 00:04:01,656
It combines the complaint, technician, status timeline, diagnostics, inspection, estimate, parts, labor, messages, invoice, and payment.

27
00:04:01,656 --> 00:04:10,409
For the Sonic, the technician enters trouble codes, rough-idle symptoms, fuel-trim data, observations, and relevant history.

28
00:04:10,409 --> 00:04:16,974
ZOL ranks possible causes, explains supporting evidence, and recommends an ordered test plan.

29
00:04:16,974 --> 00:04:29,327
Every result carries a visible warning that AI assistance requires technician verification, protecting the distinction between intake, recommendation, and confirmed diagnosis.

30
00:04:32,766 --> 00:04:44,745
The technician completes a digital inspection across engine, transmission, brakes, tires, suspension, steering, battery, fluids, lights, heating and air conditioning, exterior, interior, and safety.

31
00:04:44,745 --> 00:04:50,916
Each item is marked green, yellow, red, or not inspected, with notes, measurements, and media support.

32
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:55,575
ZOL's AI summary is grounded only in the findings that were actually entered.

33
00:04:55,575 --> 00:05:03,016
It highlights urgent issues, recommended service, maintenance, and safety concerns in language the customer can understand.

34
00:05:07,986 --> 00:05:15,167
Verified recommendations become an editable estimate with labor, parts, fees, discounts, tax, and total.

35
00:05:15,167 --> 00:05:24,765
AI can suggest repair explanations and labor or parts categories, while pricing remains clearly identified as shop-entered or demo pricing.

36
00:05:24,765 --> 00:05:35,260
The mobile customer portal brings together the original concern, inspection results, photos, diagnostic context, recommendations, and itemized estimate.

37
00:05:35,260 --> 00:05:38,436
Approval updates the repair order immediately.

38
00:05:38,436 --> 00:05:44,236
Declined items are retained for responsible future follow-up rather than being lost.

39
00:05:50,579 --> 00:05:52,765
Approved work moves into execution.

40
00:05:52,765 --> 00:06:01,133
Parts progress from needed to requested, ordered, received, installed, or returned, with supplier, quantity, cost, and customer price.

41
00:06:01,133 --> 00:06:08,814
The technician board organizes active work by assignment, urgency, approval, and parts state for desktop, tablet, or phone.

42
00:06:08,814 --> 00:06:13,685
Technicians can move jobs through repair, quality check, and ready for pickup.

43
00:06:13,685 --> 00:06:21,179
Customer messages, shop updates, and internal technician notes remain attached to the correct customer and repair order.

44
00:06:25,854 --> 00:06:32,704
When work is complete, ZOL converts the approved estimate into an invoice without re-entering line items.

45
00:06:32,704 --> 00:06:37,792
The MVP supports Stripe test mode and a clearly labeled demo-payment fallback.

46
00:06:37,792 --> 00:06:40,271
ZOL never stores raw card information.

47
00:06:40,271 --> 00:06:50,839
A successful payment records the transaction, marks the invoice paid, closes the repair order, updates service history, and creates a post-repair CRM opportunity.

48
00:06:50,839 --> 00:06:59,254
Customers can track vehicle status, review approvals, see messages, and access payment from their own mobile-friendly experience.

49
00:07:07,989 --> 00:07:19,015
ZOL's automotive CRM turns completed repairs, declined services, inspection recommendations, upcoming maintenance, and customers who have not returned into actionable follow-ups.

50
00:07:19,015 --> 00:07:23,537
AI drafts friendly outreach using only verified vehicle and service data.

51
00:07:23,537 --> 00:07:32,643
Owners can ask the controlled shop assistant about approvals, tomorrow's schedule, parts delays, technician workload, and previous recommendations.

52
00:07:32,643 --> 00:07:41,811
Tenant isolation, server-side authorization, validated AI output, Cloud SQL persistence, and replaceable integrations create a practical foundation.

53
00:07:41,811 --> 00:07:52,589
ZOL connects the complete customer-to-cash journey while helping the shop answer faster, communicate clearly, operate efficiently, and build stronger long-term relationships.

